+## Evidence573 — Lean theorem request binding and namespaced declaration checks
+
+Reconstructed Lean outcomes now enforce the same backend and theorem-proof query kind as dispatch. The published candidate at 30e1f2f8 passed 92 ordinary software cases across 19 functions, including 81 retained cases, seven backend-routing cases and four query-kind cases. Collection, execution and raw JUnit recorded the same 92 cases. A separate direct Lean 4.34.1 run made one version probe and two compilations. The root declaration `wanted` matched the expected proposition `True` and was accepted with an empty axiom report. With the same fixture source and expected proposition, `Law.wanted` had type `False → False`. Lean returned exit code 1 and the wrapper refused it. The direct run contributed zero pytest cases. Both runs closed Source and resource custody. These fixture results leave overall Phase 1 open. [Ordinary92 qualification](/tmp/Root-P1-Lean-live-ordinary92-reconcile-v596/actual-live-reconciled-P1-Lean-ordinary92-closed.json) · [Separate direct Native2 result](/tmp/Root-P1-Lean-live-ordinary92-reconcile-v596/actual-native2-output/complete-native3-direct-existing-owner-report.json) · [Code publication](/tmp/Root-P1-Lean-live-ordinary92-reconcile-v596/actual-P1-Lean-ordinary92-and-Native2-three-FF-publication.json)
